# Sub-agent isolated worktrees (Agent tool with `isolation: worktree`).
# Each agent gets its own .claude/worktrees/agent-<id>/ checkout that is
# auto-cleaned at the end of the agent run; we don't want git to track them
# while they exist.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-session kaizen scratch file. Maintained during a task, consumed by
# /after-task-dantotsus once the work merges. Local-only by design.
KAIZEN.md

# Working file for the current refactoring branch (see the PR description).
REFACTORING-BRIEF.md
.eslintcache
.eslintcache
node_modules/.cache
.stryker-tmp
reports

# The architecture maps are generated, and nothing reads the committed copy.
# `pages.yml` regenerates them before publishing, so a stale file cannot reach
# the site, and `architecture.yml` regenerates them before diffing a pull
# request. Committing them cost 9.3 MB rewritten in full on every change, and
# bought a byte gate whose only subject was its own output. The model beside
# each page is committed: it is small, it diffs as prose, and every byte of it
# comes from the working tree.
docs/architecture/*.html
